rule order_lines v1
description "The lines of an order, each with a field of every kind a line can have, some of which may be missing: how many lines are gifts and how many need care, the earliest day, the most taken off a line, how many items there are and what the lines cost"

enum size = small | large

# One line of an order. The caller passes up to three
elements lines
  label : string
  note  : string?
  size  : size
  box   : size?
  qty   : number          range >=1 <=9
  spare : number?         range >=0 <=9
  price : money[USDc]     range >=0USDc <=900USDc
  tip   : money[USDc]?    range >=0USDc <=900USDc
  off   : rate[step 1%]   range >=0% <=50%
  extra : rate[step 1%]?  range >=0% <=50%
  on    : date            range >=2026-01-01 <=2027-12-31
  upto  : date?
  gift  : bool
  rush  : bool?

# Whether a line needs care: a large one or one boxed, one with a spare, a tip, a rate taken off it
# more, a day it is held to, or a rush
table care_of
policy first
| size  | box  | spare | tip  | extra | upto | rush | -> care : bool |
| large | -    | -     | -    | -     | -    | -    | true           |
| small | none | none  | none | none  | none | none | false          |
| -     | -    | -     | -    | -     | -    | -    | true           |

count gifts over lines where gift  range >=0 <=3
count cared over lines where care  range >=0 <=3
min first over lines of on empty 2027-12-31
max most_off over lines of off empty 0%
sum items over lines of qty  range >=0 <=27
sum spent over lines of price  range >=0USDc <=2_700USDc

outputs
  gifts    : number  round down(1)
  cared    : number  round down(1)
  first    : date
  most_off : rate[step 1%]  round down(1%)
  items    : number  round down(1)
  spent    : money[USDc]  round down(1USDc)
